  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Match Lis-I with List-II.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List-1</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List-II</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A.</td>\t\t\t<td>Weak intermolecular forces of attraction</td>\t\t\t<td>I.</td>\t\t\t<td>Hexamethylenediamine<br />\t\t\t+ adipic acid</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B.</td>\t\t\t<td>Hydrogen bonding</td>\t\t\t<td>II.</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AlEt</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>TiCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C.</td>\t\t\t<td>Heavily branched polymer</td>\t\t\t<td>III.</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>chloro</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>butadiene</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D.</td>\t\t\t<td>High density polymer</td>\t\t\t<td>IV.</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Phenol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>formaldehyde</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YTVDb",
      "text": "A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wUoTD",
      "text": "A-IV, B-I, C-III, D-II",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RZ1Od",
      "text": "A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RrljU",
      "text": "A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) Weak Intermolecular Forces are present in polymer of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></math>chloro, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>butadiene.It is a monomer of neoprene which is a rubber(elastomer.).<br />(B). Hydrogen Bonding is present in NYLON<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></math> which is a polymer of Hexamethylenediamine and adipic acid. This hydrogen bonding is due to the presence of amide group.&nbsp;<br />(C) Heavily branched polymer is Bakelite which is polymer of phenol and formaldehyde. It is a crosslinked polymer.<br />(D) High density polymer(polyethylene)&nbsp;preparation requires <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Et</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>TiCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;as a catalyst (Ziegler Natta Catalyst)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
